<urn:atm:triage:finding/CI-001-AK9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "CI-001-AK9" ;
  triage:title "Mock-peer test fixtures decode AK.9 batch writes as bare WriteRequest, failing all 3 CI platforms" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root.rs mock-peer fixtures (serve_direct_peer_responses, serve_failed_then_pipelined_peer_responses) still decode inbound requests with the generic atm_core::api::decode_request, which parses the body as a bare WriteRequest. AK.9's production sender (send_peer_http_batch) always wraps writes in PeerMessageArray { messages: [...] }, which must be decoded with decode_peer_write_request (as route_peer_http_request does in production, and as tests/peer_message_array.rs/tests/resend_cache.rs already do correctly). Result: AtmError { code: MessageValidationFailed, message: \"invalid write HTTP request body: missing field `home_dir`...\" } panics at runtime_root.rs:110,171, propagating through server.join().expect(...), failing 4 tests: full_resend_page_confirms_only_its_batch_and_rearms_the_remaining_backlog, host_qualified_self_addresses_use_the_ordinary_admission_route, host_qualified_write_persists_then_confirms_direct_peer_http_delivery, peer_alias_reload_swaps_the_admission_directory_without_a_message_store_lookup. Confirmed via gh pr checks 753 (all 3 platform Test jobs FAIL, run 30965392743), independently reproduced by rust-qa-agent's cargo test --workspace run (116 passed, 4 failed), and statically confirmed by ruthless-boundary-qa via decoder trace. Fails the sprint doc's required-validation items (Regression -- replay after transport error) and the top-level just test ... pass gate." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ak" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "CI" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-05T02:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
